; Interprets: ETSI TS 183 017
;; What ETSI TS 183 017's clauses state in prose about an AVP's value or
;; presence, read by hand and pinned to the sentences read
;; (docs/constraints.md), in clause order: the Gq' procedures (clause 5),
;; the use of the base protocol (clause 6) and the commands and AVPs (clause
;; 7).
;; The document is a hand transcription (edits/transcriptions/), so the
;; quotes are held to the text of the PDF it was copied from, not to an
;; extracted source, and each block is marked as quoted from the PDF. Each
;; command prints once, under Gq's 16777222. A rule depending on a node, the
;; procedure or an earlier message is `text-only`.


;; Clause 5.1.1: an initial AAR the AAR does not tell apart from a
;; modifying one, nor a hard-state reservation or the two-phase method.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aar-hard-state-authorization-lifetime
; AVP: Authorization-Lifetime
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 5.1.1
; Versions: 3.2.1
"When requesting for Hard-state reservation, the AF shall not include an Authorization-Lifetime AVP."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aar-correlation-identifier
; AVP: User-Name
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 5.1.1
; Versions: 3.2.1
"For the purpose of access profile correlation in the A-RACF, the AF shall include within the AA-Request a correlation identifier in the form: • either of the User-Name AVP; and/or • the Globally-Unique-Address AVP."
    text-only


;; A media component's priority, as the request's (clause 7.3.9).
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: media-component-reservation-priority-default
; AVP: Reservation-Priority
; Within: Media-Component-Description
; Section: 5.1.1
; Versions: 3.2.1
"The AF may further specify the Reservation-Priority AVP in Media-Component-Description AVP(s) in order to assign priority to individual media. If the Reservation-Priority AVP is not specified the requested priority is DEFAULT (0)."
    default DEFAULT


;; Clause 5.1.2: what the initial AAR held is an earlier message.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aar-reservation-priority-unmodified
; AVP: Reservation-Priority
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 5.1.2
; Versions: 3.2.1
"If present, the Reservation-Priority AVP associated with a reservation request or a media component shall not be modified by the AF."
    text-only


;; Clause 6.5: "both" of the AF's requests, the AAR and STR, which print
;; Destination-Host optional and Destination-Realm required.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aar-destination-host
; AVP: Destination-Host
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 6.5
; Versions: 3.2.1
"The AF obtains the contact address of the SPDF for a given user via the e2 interface (ES 283 035 [13]). Both the Destination-Realm and Destination-Host AVPs shall be present in the request."
    present-if Destination-Realm


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: str-destination-host
; AVP: Destination-Host
; Command: ST-Request
; Section: 6.5
; Versions: 3.2.1
"The AF obtains the contact address of the SPDF for a given user via the e2 interface (ES 283 035 [13]). Both the Destination-Realm and Destination-Host AVPs shall be present in the request."
    present-if Destination-Realm


;; Clause 7.1.3: which of a RAR's Specific-Action AVPs hold the values no
;; kind compares.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rar-specific-actions-not-combined
; AVP: Specific-Action
; Command: RA-Request
; Section: 7.1.3
; Versions: 3.2.1
"The values INDICATION_OF_RELEASE_OF_BEARER, INDICATION_OF_SUBSCRIBER_DETACHMENT, INDICATION_OF_RESERVATION_EXPIRATION and INDICATION_OF_LOSS_OF_BEARER, INDICATION_OF_RECOVERY_OF_BEARER and INDICATION_OF_RELEASE_OF_BEARER of the Specific-Action AVP shall not be combined with each other in an Re-Auth-Request."
    text-only


;; Clause 7.3: the AVPs, read wherever the document reads them.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: binding-input-list-pairs
; AVP: Binding-Input-List
; Section: 7.3.2
; Versions: 3.2.1
"In case one of the V4-Transport-Address AVP or V6-Transport-Address AVP is such pair is unknown, an even number of list elements shall be still provided with the unknown V4-Transport-Address AVP or V6-Transport-Address AVP wild-carded."
"It shall be one pair of V4-Transport-Address AVP or V6-Transport-Address list elements in the Binding-Input-List AVP for each single Media-Component-Description AVP in an AAR."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aar-reservation-priority-default
; AVP: Reservation-Priority
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 7.3.9
; Versions: 3.2.1
"DEFAULT (0): This is the lowest level of priority. If no Reservation-Priority AVP is specified in the AA-Request, this is the priority associated with the reservation."
    default DEFAULT


;; No "assigned" at either end; the ports, "list or ranges", any.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: flow-description-restrictions
; AVP: Flow-Description
; Section: 7.3.17
; Versions: 3.2.1
"Only the Action \"permit\" shall be used."
"No \"options\" shall be used."
"The invert modifier \"!\" for addresses shall not be used."
"The keyword \"assigned\" shall not be used."
    encoding ip-filter from any to any


;; Which Flow-Grouping AVPs a message holds no kind counts.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: flow-grouping-empty-alone
; AVP: Flow-Grouping
; Section: 7.3.18
; Versions: 3.2.1
"A Flow-Grouping AVP containing no Flows AVP shall not be supplied together with other Flow-Grouping AVP(s)."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: flow-usage-default
; AVP: Flow-Usage
; Section: 7.3.22
; Versions: 3.2.1
"NO_INFORMATION is the default value."
    default NO_INFORMATION


;; How many Codec-Data AVPs a body holds no kind counts, and an offer from
;; an answer no kind reads.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: media-component-codec-data
; AVP: Codec-Data
; Within: Media-Component-Description
; Section: 7.3.26
; Versions: 3.2.1
"Each Media-Component-Description AVP shall contain either zero, or one, or two Codec-Data AVPs."
"If the Media-Component-Description AVP contains two Codec-Data AVPs, one of them shall represent an SDP offer and the other one the corresponding SDP answer."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sip-forking-indication-default
; AVP: SIP-Forking-Indication
; Section: 7.3.32
; Versions: 3.2.1
"SINGLE_DIALOGUE (0) - This value is used to indicate that the Diameter session relates to a single SIP dialogue. This is the default value applicable if the AVP is omitted."
    default SINGLE_DIALOGUE
